  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral response to support IDP and POC sites through provision of water, sanitation and hygiene and camp coordination and camp managementservices in Bentiu and Malakal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rubkona and Malakal Counties are facing critical water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) needs having been classified as Band A locations by the Needs Analysis Working Group (January 2025), indicating extreme humanitarian conditions. The situation is further exacerbated by an ongoing cholera outbreak. Clean water access and wastewater management systems are under immense strain. This proposal seeks to sustain critical WASH and camp coordination and camp management (CCCM) services for internally displaced persons (IDPs) in Bentiu IDP Camp and Malakal Protection of Civilians (PoC) site, amid deteriorating humanitarian conditions, the ongoing cholera outbreak, and escalating funding gaps.</narrative>
  </description>
